{#
  The error view (FSD §8.5, §12). "Kein Modus, sondern das Ergebnis von
  Kapitel 12: eine schlichte, gut lesbare Seite mit Fehlertext und Zeitpunkt."

  Shape [Festlegung P11, 2026-08-21]: **sentence · time · one technical line.**
  The sentence carries the message across the room, the time says how long the
  wall has been standing still, and the technical line is what saves a walk to
  the computer — it names the view and the exception, nothing more. Everything
  else stays in the status sensor and the add-on log.

  Layout follows FSD §7 and stays far inside it: nothing below 32 px, no rule
  thinner than 3 px, no gradient. Flat white with black text on purpose — white
  and black are two of the six Spectra primaries, so this page carries **no
  dither raster at all** and is the most legible surface the panel can show.
  The red is the palette's own red (220,30,30) rather than a chosen one; any
  other red would only be dithered back into this one.

  Deliberately dependency-free: no photo, no file:// subresource, no font
  beyond DejaVu. This page must render when everything else has failed.
#}<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{ language }}">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <title>ePaperEngine</title>
    <style>
      html,
      body {
        margin: 0;
        padding: 0;
        width: 2560px;
        height: 1440px;
        overflow: hidden;
        background: #fff;
        color: #000;
        font-family: "DejaVu Sans", sans-serif;
      }
      main {
        box-sizing: border-box;
        width: 2560px;
        height: 1440px;
        /* The 80 px margin FSD §7 measured its type sizes against. */
        padding: 160px 160px 120px;
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        justify-content: center;
      }
      .mark {
        font-size: 40px;
        font-weight: bold;
        letter-spacing: 6px;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        color: #dc1e1e;
      }
      .rule {
        height: 6px;
        background: #dc1e1e;
        margin: 28px 0 64px;
      }
      h1 {
        margin: 0;
        font-size: 104px;
        font-weight: bold;
        line-height: 1.15;
      }
      .since {
        margin-top: 40px;
        font-size: 56px;
      }
      .technical {
        margin-top: 80px;
        padding-top: 36px;
        border-top: 3px solid #000;
        font-family: "DejaVu Sans Mono", monospace;
        font-size: 36px;
        line-height: 1.4;
        /* Three lines is the budget. An exception message can be arbitrarily
           long, and a page that grows until it overflows the canvas would push
           the sentence off the top — the one part that has to be readable. */
        max-height: 151px;
        overflow: hidden;
        word-break: break-word;
      }
      .hint {
        margin-top: 64px;
        font-size: 36px;
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <div class="mark">ePaperEngine</div>
      <div class="rule"></div>
      <h1>{{ t("error.headline") }}</h1>
      {% if since %}<div class="since">{{ t("error.since", at=since) }}</div>{% endif %}
      <div class="technical">{{ technical }}</div>
      <div class="hint">{{ t("error.hint") }}</div>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
